      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I haven't reuploaded my ava for some time, so mabye some weeks (so old version of av 3.0 SDK).\nSometimes, when I change active meshes on it (different clothes settings - animator states are set both to activate some and to deactivate other meshes) there is a high CHANCE game will either:\n- start terribly lagging to me\n- start terribly lagging to SOMEONE in the instance (random)\n- start terribly lagging to everyone in the instance\n- will work all fine\nFPS drops without valid reason from 90 to 10-20 FPS.\nIt looks like animator is constantly trying to activate and deactivate some object, looping (my guess) which makes engine lag.\nThis was not happening before vrc update.\nNot sure if that helps but using some extra animators on the meshes itself for spawn mesh effect. However, they do not cause any issue when my ava loads as a whole - no lagging is present desptite of them being active.\nThis is definitely game/engine fault.\nResetting avatar gets rid of the lagging. Selecting default mesh state (which ones are active by default) also helps.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
